  "description": "G5: Mixed Species Group - Crown raise all trees to a minimum of 4m to provide clearance for mowing equipment.\rG6: Lombardy Poplar x10 - Reduce/pollard crowns by approximately 50% to reduce wind loading and minimise the risk of failure.\rT3: Ash x2 - Monolith both Ash trees to a height of 10m due to Ash dieback. \rT10: Weeping Willow - Re-pollard back to previous pollard points.\rT11: Atlas Cedar - Fell to ground level due to significant dieback.\rT12: Black Walnut - Reduce lateral branches by 2-3m to rebalance the crown and minimise the risk of failure. \rT13: Weeping Willow - Re-pollard back to previous pollard points.\rT15: Oak - Clear fallen tree and retain logs in habitat stacks. Reduce the field side of the remaining Oak crown by 2-3m to reduce overhang and provide access for mowing equipment.\rT19: Dead Elms x2 - Fell to ground level.\rT20: Dead Elms x3 - Reduce to a safe standing height to create monoliths.\rT21: Ash - Reduce low overhanging branches to provide clearance from the highway, crown raise to 2.5m over the footpath and 5.2m over the carriageway, and remove deadwood.\rT22: Dead Elm - Fell to ground level.\rT23: Leyland Cypress - Fell to ground level due to extensive decline and dieback. \rT24: Dead Sycamore - Reduce to a safe standing height to create a monolith.\rT25: Unidentified Tree - Reduce to a safe standing height and retain arisings in habitat stacks.\rT27: Unidentified Tree - Reduce to a safe standing height.",
